    <note type="translation" xml:lang="en">Ramaḍān al-Manfalūṭī, later al-Qāhirī, known as al-Mihtār (the steward). He was a rude commoner. He was born in Banī Ghālib, a village in the district of Manfalūṭ. His master promoted him, and he came to oversee the Kiswah (of the Kaaba) and other matters.</note>
